Disable GPIO5 in Linux. The M7 uses GPIO5 interrupts (ICM45686 DRDY on
GPIO5_IO11). gpio-vf610 probe writes 0 to all 32 ICRs of every bank it
binds, so each Linux boot disabled the M7's DRDY interrupt. The only
Linux reference (flexspi1 reset-gpios) is in a disabled node.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific configuration]

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx95-navqb.dts
@@ -1721,6 +1721,11 @@ &gpio2 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* M7 owns GPIO5 interrupts (ICM45686 DRDY); vf610 probe would clear all ICRs */
+&gpio5 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &vpuctrl {
 	boot = <&vpu_boot>;
 	sram = <&sram1>;
